> artifacts from being generated early is simple rarity.
>
> By the way, Vorpal Blade, as far as weapons go, isn't really that
> great.  It can behead foes roughly 5% of the time, and that's just
> about its only power besides instantly slaying Jabberwocks.

But it doesn't destroy monster inventory.  It's not great, but it's
one of the better artifact weapons--really aside from the "big 5"
you're almost as well off just using a katana or silver saber as
anything else, and I think Vorpy edges out a katana but I'd have to
think about it.

Glancing through the artifact list, Grayswandir, Excalibur, Magicbane,
Stormbringer, and Snickersnee are the only ones that are clearly
better to me.

Less clearly, I'd probably prefer frosty/firebrand, but I'd consider
them about even with Vorpy--unless I got them well enchanted early on,
when the damage output is very important.  Then I'd definitely prefer
them.

I'd prefer Mojo slightly in the early game only, but vorpy in the mid-
late game (I'd use ?enchant weapon on vorpy and switch once it was
reasonably enchanted).

I would be about even on Sunsword (surely using it if I lacked a
lamp).
The Sceptre I'd prefer but it's not worth a wish so that's pretty
useless.
Werebane I might take over Vorpy, but only because it's silver.
The Staff I'd certainly avoid.

Nothing else is very close.

I might go with a regular katana or silver saber over Vorpy (or any of
the latter group except obviously silver saber vs. werebane), except
when dealing with teleport-to-the-stairs foes.



